{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q021_nad_binding_convergent_evolution","answer":"NAD(P) binding is a biochemical capability that can evolve independently in different protein scaffolds; it does not define a single homologous lineage. In SCOPe 2.08, the NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold superfamily c.2.1 (SUNID 51735) belongs to fold c.2, whereas the NAD(P)-linked oxidoreductase superfamily c.1.7 (SUNID 51430) belongs to the TIM beta/alpha-barrel fold c.1. Both are in class c, alpha/beta proteins, but that broad architectural similarity does not establish ancestry.

This distribution supports convergent recruitment of NAD(P) binding across distinct lineages, alongside divergent evolution within homologous families and superfamilies. A SCOPe family indicates clear evolutionary relatedness; a superfamily groups families with evidence for probable common ancestry, sometimes despite weak sequence similarity. Fold membership describes shared core topology without necessarily implying homology, and class describes broad secondary-structure organization. Separate superfamilies or folds do not prove that remote ancestry is impossible, nor does classification alone establish how many independent origins occurred.

Cofactor chemistry constrains binding-site geometry, charge, hydrogen bonding, and catalytic positioning, so unrelated proteins can independently acquire similar pockets, short glycine-rich motifs, or catalytic residues. These local similarities are insufficient evidence of homology. A stronger inference requires significant sequence/profile similarity across a substantial domain, compatible overall topology and structural alignment, and conserved residue arrangements beyond the active site, ideally supported by evolutionary analysis. Shared NAD(P) binding alone cannot justify transferring substrate specificity, reaction mechanism, NAD versus NADP preference, or a whole-domain modeling template; those require additional sequence, structural, and biochemical evidence.","evidence_used":["Pretrained biological knowledge","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=NAD&mode=auto&limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.1.7","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.1.7/parents"]}]}
